   {
    "name": "Mystic Expansion",
    "compareWith": "Lucky Shot",
    "claim": "should_be_more_obscure",
    "reason": "The Y in Mystic Expansion is easy to spot, but 'Mystic' is a very common item prefix, so players will pick among many Mystic items. Making it the single most obvious answer at 10 points overstates how readily it comes to mind. Lucky Shot has a Y-heavy, memorable name that is just as likely to be typed first.",
    "outcome": "applied"
   },
   {
    "name": "Mystic Regeneration",
    "compareWith": "Mystic Burst",
    "claim": "should_be_more_obvious",
    "reason": "Mystic Regeneration is a Tier 1 Spirit item with the same 'Mystic' prefix and is a very commonly bought starter. It should be as easy to recall as Mystic Burst, so 85 pts is too obscure compared with 30.",
    "outcome": "applied"
   },
   {
    "name": "Frenzy",
    "compareWith": "Trophy Collector",
    "claim": "should_be_more_obvious",
    "reason": "Frenzy ends in Y, which makes it a one-word, easy-to-recall Y answer that is well known as a Tier 4 weapon item. At 85 pts it is placed far more obscure than Trophy Collector (60), which is a longer name where players tend to miss the Y.",
    "outcome": "applied"
   },
   {
    "name": "Intensifying Magazine",
    "compareWith": "Decay",
    "claim": "should_be_more_obscure",
    "reason": "Intensifying Magazine has no Y in the name as written, so it is unlikely to be a valid answer or to be typed at all, but if it is counted it is clearly rarer than Decay. Decay is a short, memorable name that players know well and that contains a Y at the end, so it should not sit at the same obscurity level just below. The scoring should not have Decay at 85 close to the 100 slot.",
